From: LinBox <linbox@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] LinBox box64: gate -Wno-pointer-type-mismatch to Clang (CI noise fix)

-Wno-pointer-type-mismatch is a CLANG flag; gcc prints
"cc1: note: unrecognized command-line option" noise in every CI host-smoke
build. Zero effect on the shipped binary (the rootfs framework never
passes -DCI=ON). The if(CI) block only exists since v0.3.2; on v0.3.0 the
dry-run fails and this file is skipped - harmless.
The hunk headers carry v0.4.4 line numbers; patch locates the
(unique) anchors by scanning, so line drift across tags is fine. A hunk that
cannot find its anchors fails the dry-run and is skipped whole
(patchOptional=1 in build.sh) - it is NEVER force-placed at a wrong offset.

---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -321,3 +321,5 @@
 if(CI)
-    add_definitions(-Wno-pointer-type-mismatch)
+    # LinBox: -Wno-pointer-type-mismatch is a CLANG flag; gcc does not know it
+    # (cc1 "unrecognized" note, seen live in CI host smoke) - clang-only gate.
+    add_definitions(-Wno-pointer-type-mismatch)
 endif()
